# Ponytail on this production site

Ponytail is an **agent coding ruleset**, not an npm/runtime dependency. Do not install it into `package.json`, PostCSS, or the Next build. Production impact = smaller, safer diffs agents ship.

## Stack constraints (do not fight them)

- Next.js 14 App Router + React 18 + Tailwind 3.4 + existing Framer Motion / GSAP / Lucide only when already used nearby.
- Prefer reuse: `components/ui/*`, `components/sections/*`, `components/layout/*`, CSS tokens in `app/globals.css`.
- No new UI libraries, icon packs, date pickers, or CSS frameworks for tasks this stack already covers.

## Ladder examples for this repo

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — new dep + wrapper for a simple control
import DatePicker from "react-datepicker";

// ✅ GOOD — native platform feature (ponytail rung 4)
<input type="date" className="..." />
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — new button primitive
<button className="rounded-full bg-purple-600 ...">Get quote</button>

// ✅ GOOD — reuse installed pattern
import PrimaryButton from "@/components/ui/PrimaryButton";
```

## Production hygiene

- Ship the shortest diff that preserves a11y, contact/API validation, and existing brand tokens (`navy`, `solar-gold`, spacing CSS vars).
- Do not redesign pages or “modernize” Tailwind when fixing bugs.
- Mark intentional shortcuts with `// ponytail: <ceiling> → <upgrade>`.
